  "text_pages": [
    "International Relations\nI\nnternational\nR\nelations\nLOGIN\nINTRODUCTION\nWelcome Message\nPartners\nContact us\nDirections\nINBOUND\nExchange/Visiting Program\nOUTBOUND\n교환/방문학생\n국외연수\n단기파견\n체험후기\nNEWS\nNews\nI\nnternational\nR\nelations\nSEOULTECH\n|\nOIA\n|\nLOGIN\n학과 메뉴\nINTRODUCTION\nINBOUND\nOUTBOUND\nNEWS\nWelcome Message\nPartners\nContact us\nDirections\nExchange/Visiting Program\n교환/방문학생\n국외연수\n단기파견\n체험후기\nNews\nExchange/Visiting Program\nINBOUND\nINTRODUCTION\nINBOUND\nOUTBOUND\nNEWS\nExchange/Visiting Program\nExchange/Visiting Program\nINBOUND\nExchange/Visiting Program\nINTRODUCTION\nINBOUND\nOUTBOUND\nNEWS\nExchange/Visiting Program\nOverview\nCalendar\nCourse\nVisa\nCampus life & Living\nAcademic Credit System\nExchange/Visiting Program\n홈\nINBOUND\nExchange/Visiting Program\nVisa\nOverview\nCalendar\nCourse\nVisa\nCampus life & Living\nAcademic Credit System\n□\nApply for a Student Visa\n○\nA student visa (D-2)\nis required to study in Korea for students who are not of Korean nationality.\n○ Visa Type:\n- Partner University student:\nD-2-6\nvisa\n- Non-partner University student:\nD-2-8\nvisa\n○ Please contact your\nnearest Korean Embassy or consulate\nfor more detailed information on the visa application process.\n○ Be aware that students\ncannot change their visitor visa to a student visa in Korea\n.\nYou should apply for a\nstudent visa (D-2-6 / D-2-8)\n.\n○ As of June 2022, the Ministry of Justice introduced new regulations that include a strengthened immigration policy.\nThis requires exchange students from non-OECD countries to submit\nadditional materials\n:\n- Students from\nOECD\ncountries: Normally, three documents (Certificate of Admission, Acceptance Letter, and Certificate of Business Registration) will be sufficient to apply for a student visa (D-2-6 / D-2-8).\n- Students from\nnon-OECD\ncountries: Due to the strengthened immigration policy by the Ministry of Justice, additional materials are required even for exchange students:\n*\nA Certificate of Bank Statement (Balance)\n: The bank statement should cover your exchange study semester living costs (USD 4,000 for one semester / USD 8,000 for one academic year).\n*\nA Certificate of Enrollment from Your Home University\n: It must be Apostilled or notarized by the Embassy of Korea in your country.\n[개인정보처리방침]\n|\n[이메일무단수집거부]\nTel : +82-2-970-9206~7 Fax : +82-2-970-9229\nCopyright (c) SEOUL NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY. All Rights Reserved."
